, becoming a cultural icon referenced in media and discussions on mental health."}], "places": [{"name": "Oslo, Norway", "role": "Artistic Hub"}, {"name": "Berlin, Germany", "role": "Cultural Influence"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Artistic Inspiration"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: The Scream", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "the-scream"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q471379", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Scream"], "tags": ["group of paintings", "Paintings & Visual Art", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "The Scream left a notable mark on Modern history, documented across 78 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The Scream significantly shaped the development of modern art and influenced discussions around mental health, with its themes resonating through art and culture, impacting how emotional experiences are expressed artistically.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-08T21:17:52Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27167444875", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Group of paintings by edvard munch Created by Edvard Munch. Created c. 1893.", "newValue": "The Scream, a series of iconic paintings created by the Norwegian artist Edvard Munch between 1893 and 1910, represents a profound exploration of existential angst and human emotion. Particularly notable is the 1893 version, housed at the National Gallery in Oslo, which has become a symbol of modern existential crisis and anxiety. This artwork emerged during a time of profound societal change in Europe, marked by rapid industrialization and the psychological upheaval that accompanied it. Munch's innovative use of color and form to convey emotion has had a lasting impact on the trajectory of modern art, influencing generations of artists and shaping cultural discourse around mental health and the human condition.

The creation of The Scream was influenced by Munch's own life experiences, including the early deaths of his mother and father and his struggles with mental illness. The painting itself features a ghostly figure standing on a bridge against a tumultuous sky, capturing an intense moment of panic and despair. Munch produced several versions of this work, including paintings, pastels, and lithographs, each reinforcing the central theme of anxiety. The variations highlight Munch's exploration of the fragility of the human psyche, making it a pivotal work in the Symbolist movement and an early precursor to Expressionism.

The legacy of The Scream extends far beyond the art world; it has become a cultural icon, referenced in various forms of media and popular culture. Its imagery has been appropriated in everything from advertising to film, demonstrating its profound resonance with the human experience. The painting has inspired an array of interpretations and discussions around mental health, existentialism, and the nature of fear in the modern age, making it relevant to contemporary audiences. As Munch himself said, 'I felt that there was a great scream in nature,' reflecting the universal struggle that continues to echo through time."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T21:17:52Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27167444875", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The rise of modern existential philosophy in the late 19th century influenced Munch's thematic choices.", "Industrialization and urbanization in Europe led to increased feelings of anxiety and alienation among individuals.", "Munch's personal experiences with loss and mental illness shaped his artistic expression, particularly in The Scream."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T21:17:52Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27167444875", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["The Scream has become an enduring symbol of existential angst and human emotion in art and culture.", "It influenced the development of the Expressionist movement, encouraging artists to explore emotional depth in their work.", "The painting's iconic status has led to widespread discussions about mental health and the human condition in contemporary society."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T21:17:52Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27167444875", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "the-scream", "sourceName": "The Scream", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-modern", "targetNa